1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,216
A Microsoft AI Foundry, Snowflake and Databricks POC

2
00:00:16,416 --> 00:00:39,184
Side effects are mentioned where pharmacovigilance does not look

3
00:00:39,384 --> 00:01:04,120
The clock starts when anyone in the company first hears of the case

4
00:01:04,320 --> 00:01:26,248
Two distinct jobs: did PV receive everything, and is there anything nobody passed on?

5
00:01:26,448 --> 00:01:55,576
Spontaneous or solicited changes what "reportable" means

6
00:01:55,776 --> 00:02:10,504
Re-read every record. Keep what PV never received.

7
00:02:10,704 --> 00:02:40,432
Step 1 · Screen: adverse event, special situation, or nothing for PV?

8
00:02:40,632 --> 00:03:06,088
Step 2 · Extract the case facts, every one with its quote

9
00:03:06,288 --> 00:03:44,224
Step 3 · Deterministic rules: no model decides a deadline

10
00:03:44,424 --> 00:04:14,920
Step 4 · Match: has pharmacovigilance already got this case?

11
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:39,904
Why patient initials matter: 0.69 to 0.84 and 0.84 to 0.96

12
00:04:40,104 --> 00:05:31,192
Every disagreement was classified; the fixes came from the causes

13
00:05:31,392 --> 00:05:56,776
Step 5 · A finding with a priority and a proposed intake package

14
00:05:56,976 --> 00:06:18,352
Step 6 · Reconcile what vendors sent against what PV received

15
00:06:18,552 --> 00:06:45,448
The reviewer works a prioritised queue in a five-page app

16
00:06:45,648 --> 00:07:09,976
Confirm day 0, choose the outcome, record the decision

17
00:07:10,176 --> 00:07:33,400
Three systems, one repository, everything deployed by script

18
00:07:33,600 --> 00:08:00,448
Ten schemas: sources, the safety database, results, review, audit, evaluation

19
00:08:00,648 --> 00:08:28,672
The agent's credential can read six secure views and nothing else

20
00:08:28,872 --> 00:08:47,800
One Foundry project, two providers, no API keys

21
00:08:48,000 --> 00:09:15,784
The matching agent is a hosted agent in Foundry Agent Service

22
00:09:15,984 --> 00:09:37,432
Secrets never sit in the image: a project connection injects the agent's key at start

23
00:09:37,632 --> 00:10:17,608
The sweep runs unattended as a container job, and nothing fails silently

24
00:10:17,808 --> 00:10:40,096
Source text is untrusted: read-only tools, validation twice, content filters

25
00:10:40,296 --> 00:11:26,824
Least privilege: seven roles, and no run-time role can update or delete

26
00:11:27,024 --> 00:11:55,792
The same platform on Azure Databricks: same tables, results copied, nothing recomputed

27
00:11:55,992 --> 00:12:07,528
Same numbers on both platforms

28
00:12:07,728 --> 00:13:23,752
Why it is built this way: fifteen decisions, each with its alternative and its reason

29
00:13:23,952 --> 00:13:55,408
One command creates Azure: Foundry, models, registry, identities, Key Vault, the job, the Databricks workspace

30
00:13:55,608 --> 00:14:27,376
Five commands build the data platform: keys, bootstrap, migrations, load, app

31
00:14:27,576 --> 00:14:55,720
Build the image, deploy the hosted agents, put the keys in Key Vault, start a sweep

32
00:14:55,920 --> 00:15:17,608
CI on every push; deployment is a manual workflow with OIDC and no stored secrets

33
00:15:17,808 --> 00:15:42,064
Develop and evaluate on a laptop: the same runner over a local file

34
00:15:42,264 --> 00:16:29,872
450 synthetic records with known answers, anchored on real cases, validated

35
00:16:30,072 --> 00:16:45,208
Custom evaluators in Foundry grade routing, matching and causality

36
00:16:45,408 --> 00:17:13,744
Measured, not assumed

37
00:17:13,944 --> 00:17:49,960
Same code through Anthropic's API and through Foundry: within half a point

38
00:17:50,160 --> 00:18:06,736
What the numbers do not say

39
00:18:06,936 --> 00:18:57,784
The business case: 327 hours a month by hand, 24 to 39 with the sweep

40
00:18:57,984 --> 00:19:49,192
Residency: three options, and the decision the sponsor is asked to make

41
00:19:49,392 --> 00:20:08,560
From proof of concept to production

42
00:20:08,760 --> 00:20:56,248
Everything in the box

43
00:20:56,448 --> 00:21:11,416
github.com/cesarzea/pharmacovigilance-sweep
